  "references": [
    "•Usually outpatient.",
    "Feldman EC, Nelson RW. Periparturient •Spontaneous remission—occurs in most patients before or at next cycle; medical therapy is generally not warranted. •Medical—for rare development of anemia, metritis, or peritonitis.",
    "Johnston SD, Root Kustritz MV, Olson PNS. •Severely affected patients—may require blood transfusion (rare). •Warn owner of the rare possibility of excessive hemorrhage; instruct owner to monitor mucous membrane color. •Ovariohysterectomy—curative; treatment",
    "Voorhorst MJ, van Brederode JC, Albersof choice if future breeding not desired. •Surgical curettage of subinvoluted sites—may also be performed; effectiveness unknown."
  ],
